The first gate run exposed a performance bug in the checker instrumentation, not the construction: `verify()` was re-validating all 3,232 instance edges for every one of 200,000 random candidates. I’m moving instance-integrity checks to generation/self-test and keeping candidate verification proportional to the submitted witness, which is the intended cheap-check model.
